Service: To cultivate the next generation in coding

My goal is to foster the next generation of technologists with an emphasis on ethical thinking and creative innovation.
My experience as a Peer Tutor and Coding Camp Assistant required me to demystify complex topics in Data Structures, Algorithms, and introductory programming for learners of all levels—from young children to university students. This practice in translating technical concepts for diverse audiences has become a cornerstone of my collaborative approach.
Looking forward, I intend to leverage the discipline and leadership training I have gained in the Corps of Cadets and Corps Cybersecurity Unit to organize structured mentorship programs. I aim to create peer-led study groups that not only assist with coursework but also help underclassmen navigate the rigors of balancing academic excellence with regimental duties. I believe that being an effective programmer extends beyond personal technical skill; it involves building a community where knowledge is shared freely and supportively.


